{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_trait`\n\n`trust_but_verify::graph::CriterionPath` represents a\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.question_path`:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Defined in trust_but_verify::graph.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\npub struct CriterionPath {\n    segments: Vec<String>,\n}\n\nimpl CriterionPath {\n    /// Construct a question's path, preserving segment order and boundaries.\n    /// Empty paths and empty segments are valid.\n    pub fn new(segments: Vec<String>) -> Self;\n\n    /// Read the ordered path segments.\n    pub fn segments(&self) -> &[String];\n}\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Identify this question relative to its source node.\n    fn criterion_path(&self) -> CriterionPath;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nIts identity is stable across runs and changes to input contents. Different\nquestions that need independent assessments have different paths; nested paths\ncan distinguish several questions within one area.\n\nThe complete identity is the pair of source node and criterion path.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_path`. The marked tests cover each obligation below. I didn't read implementation source.\n\n**Type shape and read-only access.** The struct's doctest in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[CriterionPath]` is a `compile_fail` that tries `path.segments.clear()`. It checks that the `segments` field is private. The same item carries the {test} reference.\n\n**`new` preserves order and boundaries; empty paths and segments are valid.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criterion_paths_preserve_hierarchy_empty_segments_order_and_unicode]` builds `[]`, `[\"\"]`, `[\"a\",\"b\"]`, `[\"a/b\"]`, `[\"b\",\"a\"]`, and two Unicode forms, `é` and `e\\u{301}`. It asserts that every pair is unequal.\n- A `new` that sorted, merged or split segments, or collapsed empty ones, would fail those pair checks.\n- The same test round-trips each path through serde JSON and checks `Hash` is deterministic.\n\n**`segments()` accessor.**\n- The marked storage test calls `store.record_path(...)`, which reads `segments()`. It asserts exact on-disk paths for nested, empty, `/`, control-character and Unicode segments. Those expected paths show that segment order and boundaries come back unchanged.\n- Other tests in the crate assert `.segments()` directly, but they aren't marked. This is not an assertion gap.\n\n**`criterion_path()` on the trait.**\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts `value.criterion_path() == path([\"behavior\"])`. It does the same for the loaded record.\n- It stores and loads records under that path.\n- The `Review` criterion in the test returns its configured path from `criterion_path`.\n\n**Stable across runs.** Serde round-trip, deterministic hashing, and store-then-load of the same descriptor by path all show the identity is reproducible. In that test, a later `verify` with a different answer but the same path still addresses the same saved record.\n\n**Different questions have different paths; nested paths distinguish questions.**\n- The criteria test persists `behavior`, `structure` and `text` separately. It then checks the records are independent (the counters show 4 executions and 3 writes, and each record holds its own output).\n- `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` asserts that a record under `[]` is not loaded for the `[\"new\"]` path.\n- The storage test separates `[\"b\",\"c\"]` from `[\"c\"]` in each pairing.\n\n**Complete identity is the pair of source node and criterion path.**\n- `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` loads with `Node(2)` and the same path and gets `None`.\n- The storage test varies (source, criterion) boundary placements, such as `a|b,c` against `a,b|c`. It checks each pair maps to a distinct record file that loads back independently.\n\n**Stability across changes to input contents.** `criterion_path(&self)` cannot see node contents. The tests keep the path constant while answers and dependencies change, and a record is still found afterwards. I do not count the lack of a dedicated content-change test as a gap.\n\nAll the {test} references are on tests whose assertions enforce these outcomes.",
  "references": "334c080b5dacbcccf1d46bb1032ab893d7ce979372d6904c7307215463071fbe",
